> equiv q q0
q and q0 are equal on the domain of q (exhaustive)
> equiv q0 q
q0 and q differ at 256 points, e.g. x=-128, y=0: 7 vs undefined
> add(x: u8, y: u8) = x + y
> twice(x: i32) = x + x
> sub(x: i32, y: i32) = y - x
> wrap add
wrap analysis of add:
  x + y   (u8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 32640 points, e.g. x=255, y=1
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 16384 points, e.g. x=127, y=1
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 32640 points, e.g. x=255, y=1
  over all 65536 points of the domain
