  x + x   (i32)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 32976 points, e.g. x=-2147483648
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 32964 points, e.g. x=-2147483648  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 32964 points, e.g. x=-2147483648
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4294967296 points); not exhaustive
